```c
size_t available_bytes = pool_size - data_area_start;
if (current_used + data_len > available_bytes) {
    return -1;
}
```

This ensures the function returns `-1` before copying if there's insufficient space, preventing the write past the pool boundary. The change aligns with the algorithm specification step 4: *"Fail if used + data_len > available bytes"*.

